id: pm-github-xhtp
title: Explain privacy matches and distinguish bare-root regex literals during gated sync
description: "Fix GitHub issue #160: the public pm-web issue 218 regex literal is classified as an absolute host root. Preserve path refusals in every imported field, provide safe match evidence, and verify no-git refusal."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog-unreleased,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#160"
created_at: "2026-10-21T04:40:30.603Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T08:27:37.701Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The public pm-web issue 218 text and comments import through ordinary and atomic gated modes.; Actual host paths in titles, bodies, comments and labels are refused before tracker mutation.; Refusals identify the item and published field with a safe excerpt and character offset.; A real plain tracker outside Git receives a clear refusal with no imported item writes.; Behavioral reverts fail the targeted regressions and npm and Bun release gates retain all original thresholds."
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T04:41:06.116Z",codex-agent,"Read issue #160 and fetched pm-web issue 218 plus both public comments using read-only GitHub REST calls. The body regex literal produces one absolute-host-path match at body offset 2229; SHA-256 71708eb255bc230cd7c91dd26f7667a7b9386a2dc1f09756555c2c5c8bdc3c47 exactly matches the failed workflow receipt. The match is a bare root token inside JavaScript regex source, not an importer-added path or a GitHub URL. Plan: narrowly distinguish that regex syntax, add redacted match evidence to both report formats, and test real temporary tracker imports plus missing-repository refusal."
  "2026-10-21T04:44:12.762Z",codex-agent,"Implemented a narrow exception for bare root tokens followed by JavaScript regex source and test/exec invocation. Slash-separated paths remain scanned, including inside regex source. Reports now carry match_offset and a redacted excerpt; host paths reveal only the root initial and other findings use a fixed redaction marker. Read-only public fixture imports pass in ordinary and atomic modes; adversarial title/body/comment/label paths fail before any tracker mutation. Strengthened the existing no-git test to initialize a real plain tracker with a Git discovery ceiling."
  "2026-10-21T04:44:57.092Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: restoring only HOST_PATH_RULES makes both the real public issue import regression and the bare-root regex regression fail (2/2 failures), retaining the exact reported hash. Restoring only scanChangeFile, runTrackerGate and formatGateReport makes both the redacted evidence regression and the adversarial imported-field diagnostics regression fail (2/2 failures). Restored the fix after each experiment. Baseline before edits also failed both new import tests. No history was rewritten."
  "2026-10-21T04:47:01.359Z",codex-agent,"Review tightened regex recognition to require an expression boundary and forbid crossing quotes, escapes, newlines or additional slashes. Added quoted-path and shell-text adversarial cases. Linked tests ran through pm test --run --progress: 2/2 commands passed (3 import/no-git tests and 12 scanner/input tests). The tracker has test-result tracking disabled, so results are recorded here rather than changing project policy. Final scanner-only revert now restores scanLineForRuleHits; evidence-function revert remains independently verified."
  "2026-10-21T04:51:40.978Z",codex-agent,"The first clean-HOME release gate passed typecheck/build/docstrings/lint/duplication/privacy (6121 objects), then test compilation found two missing test type updates. Updated the manually constructed GateFinding fixture with match evidence and narrowed the import result before asserting imported count. Thresholds and runtime behavior are unchanged. Final scanLineForRuleHits-only behavioral revert independently failed both relevant regressions (2/2), and the fixed scanner was restored."
  "2026-10-21T05:15:04.991Z",codex-agent,"Stopped an intermediate full coverage run after 126 reported passes and no reported failures to harden the new helper against long malformed whitespace. The regex now consumes exactly one leading whitespace character before its remaining source class, avoiding overlapping whitespace quantifiers. Added a 100000-space malformed-source case and a multiple-space valid-regex case. Restarting the complete clean-environment release gate on the final scanner; no thresholds, pins or source exclusions changed."
  "2026-10-21T07:11:56.552Z",codex-agent,"Complete clean-environment npm run release:check passed: 983/983 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips. Exact coverage across all 16 authored modules: lines and statements 11086/11086, functions 303/303, branches 3539/3539. Duplication zero, production audit zero vulnerabilities, privacy audit passed, package dry-run and canonical changelog check passed, release publish attestation passed. The real public issue import, adversarial field refusals, native Bun repeat acceptance and no-git refusal all passed in the full run. Isolated-global strict health and validation passed, with zero history drift. Starting the Bun release gate on unchanged executable source and tests."
  "2026-10-21T08:27:35.749Z",codex-agent,"Complete clean-environment bun run release:check passed: 983/983 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips. All 16 authored modules again measured exact coverage: lines and statements 11086/11086, functions 303/303, branches 3539/3539. Every remaining release gate passed at original thresholds, including privacy, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, packaging, changelog and publish attestation. Final pm test --run --progress rerun passed both linked commands (3 import/no-git tests plus 12 scanner/input tests). Test-result persistence remains disabled by existing policy, so results are preserved in comments. Final isolated-global strict health and validation passed with zero history drift; only existing advisory tracker warnings remain. Ready for PR review. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or package release."
